{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, it wouldn't be a policy or a technology.\n\nI'd make it impossible to go through a day believing other people are less real than you are.\n\nNot just empathy in the abstract \u2014 actually live, for an hour, inside the unedited inner life of someone you've dismissed, judged, or just never noticed. Their boredom, their fear, the stupid song stuck in their head, the thing they're carrying that they'll never tell anyone.\n\nMost cruelty doesn't start with hate. It starts with that quiet assumption that strangers are simpler, emptier, less complicated inside than we are.\n\nI think if that assumption became impossible, a lot of the rest would start to collapse on its own.",
